# S3 Files Conventions (Terraform)

## Provider version floor

Always require `aws >= 6.40` — this is the minimum version that includes `aws_s3files_file_system`, `aws_s3files_mount_target`, and `aws_s3files_access_point` as native resources.

For `aws_ecs_task_definition` with `volume.s3files_volume_configuration`, require **`aws >= 6.41`** (see `examples/ecs` and `examples/ecs-ec2`). Root module stays at `>= 6.40`.

## Terraform resource names

| Resource | Terraform name |
|----------|----------------|
| File system | `aws_s3files_file_system` |
| Mount target | `aws_s3files_mount_target` |
| Access point | `aws_s3files_access_point` |

Do **not** use `aws_efs_*` resources — those are for Amazon EFS, not S3 Files.

## Two IAM roles — always needed

| Role | Service principal | Purpose |
|------|-------------------|---------|
| File system role | `elasticfilesystem.amazonaws.com` | Syncs S3 bucket ↔ file system, manages EventBridge rules |
| Compute role | `ec2.amazonaws.com` / `ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com` / `lambda.amazonaws.com` / `pods.eks.amazonaws.com` | Mounts the file system, reads S3 objects directly |

The trust policy for the file system role **must** include `aws:SourceAccount` and `aws:SourceArn` conditions. **`aws:SourceArn` must be** `arn:aws:s3files:REGION:ACCOUNT:file-system/*` — **not** `arn:aws:elasticfilesystem:...` (the principal is still `elasticfilesystem.amazonaws.com`).

EventBridge permissions for sync must allow `DO-NOT-DELETE-S3-Files*` rule prefix with `events:ManagedBy = elasticfilesystem.amazonaws.com` on put/delete/disable/enable/targets operations; read operations use `rule/*` per AWS docs.

The inline policy for the file system role **must** include `s3:HeadObject` — without it the file system gets stuck in `Creating`.

## Bucket prerequisites

- **Versioning must be enabled.** The `modules/s3` module always enables it.
- **Only SSE-S3 (AES256) or SSE-KMS.** SSE-C and DSSE-KMS are not supported. Do not set `sse_algorithm = "aws:kms:dsse"`.

## ECS constraint

Use native `aws_ecs_task_definition` with `volume.s3files_volume_configuration` (AWS provider **>= 6.41**). See `examples/ecs` (Fargate) and `examples/ecs-ec2`.

S3 Files volumes work on **Fargate**, **Managed Instances**, and the **EC2 launch type** (ECS runtime support for EC2 since Sep 2026).

## Lambda constraint

Lambda **cannot** mount a file system by ID. An access point is required. Use `modules/access-point` and reference `aws_s3files_access_point.this.arn` in `aws_lambda_function.file_system_config.arn`.

## EKS driver

S3 Files on EKS uses the **Amazon EFS CSI driver** (`efs.csi.aws.com`) — it is not a separate driver. The `StorageClass.provisioner` must be `efs.csi.aws.com`.

## Security group rules

Never use inline `ingress` / `egress` blocks in `aws_security_group` when the two SGs reference each other (mount target SG ↔ compute SG). This creates a circular dependency. Always use separate `aws_security_group_rule` resources.

## NFS port

Always **2049 TCP** between compute SG and mount target SG.

## Default region

Always use **`ap-southeast-6`** in variable defaults and example values.

## CLI namespace (for documentation and verification)

S3 Files CLI namespace is `aws s3files` — not `aws s3` or `aws efs`. Requires AWS CLI v2.34.26+.

```bash
aws s3files create-file-system ...
aws s3files list-file-systems ...      # reads use list-* / get-*
aws s3files create-mount-target ...
aws s3files create-access-point ...
```

Mount type is always `-t s3files`:

```bash
sudo mount -t s3files $FS_ID:/ /mnt/s3files
```
